    "narrative": "For LawDog today, we are prioritizing power-sprint utility to navigate a slate featuring several elite arms. **Cal Raleigh** (77.68) stands as our premier play; he benefits from an optimal matchup against Sugano\u2019s 4.91 xERA and a stadium environment that juices his output by 14%. Similarly, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (66.56) is a lock; while he faces an average arm in Perkins, his consistent hitting and the slight uptick in stolen base potential against a slow-delivering pitcher make him an elite engine for our 5x5 categories. **Bryce Harper** (65.78) and **JJ Bleday** (65.61) round out our core, with the latter benefiting from a favorable 14% platoon edge against Peterson, positioning both to anchor our production in runs and RBI.\n\nThe optimization process was most contentious at the fringes, specifically regarding **Jung Hoo Lee** (39.12). He fell just short of the 40.0 floor, primarily due to a 19% downgrade against Dreyer\u2019s effective stuff and a significant platoon disadvantage. As a result, we are leaning into the high-upside potential of **Dylan Beavers** (56.73) and **Jeremiah Jackson** (54.12) against Misiorowski. While Misiorowski\u2019s 2.32 xERA poses a significant threat, the projected batting order lead-off roles for both **Dylan Beavers** and **Jeremiah Jackson** provide enough opportunity to justify their starts over the safer, but lower-ceiling, profile of **Jung Hoo Lee**.\n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the lineup status for **Jeremiah Jackson** and **Dylan Beavers**, as both are currently \"Lineup Pending.\" If either drops from the lead-off spot, their value\u2014driven by the +10% order bonus\u2014will crater. Furthermore, we are aggressively avoiding risks like **Zack Gelof** (40.16), whose score is suppressed by the elite 2.91 xERA of Williams and an unfavorable platoon split. While **Justin Crawford** (53.31) remains in the lineup for his speed profile, his ninth-spot placement is a drag on his efficiency; he is essentially a volatility play to keep our SB category competitive while we wait for more favorable matchups for the rest of the squad.",
